&lt;li&gt;Credibility in partner discovery, executive pitches, and solution planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial judgment that connects product roadmaps to adoption, payment volume, and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A founder or GM mindset that moves from ambiguous strategy to launch-level detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and influence across technical, business, risk, compliance, and external teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech, payments, issuing, or embedded-finance experience is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $280,000 - $350,000.&amp;nbsp; However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://brex.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://brex.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;brex.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world&#39;s best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product at Brex&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product team is at the forefront of Brex&#39;s mission to empower employees anywhere to make better financial decisions. With a deep understanding of the business, we identify and scope the most impactful opportunities for Brex to tackle. We align cross-functional teams—including Engineering, Legal, Compliance, and Design—on key decisions, set strategy, and drive products from inception to launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Processing a single expense is becoming commoditized. Managing expenses across an enterprise is not. Companies must distribute cards broadly while controlling risk, documenting transactions, enforcing policy, routing approvals, preparing for audit, and producing ERP-ready records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Staff Product Manager for Expenses, you will turn that complexity into one intelligent system for employees, managers, finance teams, and accountants. You will lead the strategy across documentation, policy, compliance, approvals, substantiation, audit, and accounting readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will align specialized product teams across Engineering, Design, Risk, Compliance, Accounting, and GTM. Using AI and automation, you will eliminate routine work, surface meaningful exceptions, help finance teams close faster, and build capabilities that win major enterprise relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you’ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in either our San Francisco, Seattle, or New York office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end strategy for enterprise expense management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unify documentation, policy, compliance, approvals, substantiation, audit, and ERP readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the systems, data models, configurations, and controls complex enterprises require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align specialized product teams around the complete expense lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to automate routine work and route only judgment-heavy exceptions to people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design to make sophisticated enterprise workflows intuitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align Engineering, Design, Risk, Compliance, Accounting, Sales, and Customer Success around enterprise outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own adoption, workflow completion, manual-work reduction, close speed, retention, and software revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex enterprise workflow or systems products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency in backend systems, data models, integrations, and configurable product architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting extensive customer permutations without sacrificing usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to unite multiple domains under one strategy and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer and Design judgment across employee, manager, finance, and accounting experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concrete judgment about where AI should remove work and where human review matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional influence and an understanding of how product capabilities affect enterprise sales and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expense management experience is preferred; accounting, ERP, procurement, compliance, or adjacent enterprise-software experience can substitute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $240,000 - $300,000.&amp;nbsp; However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please be aware, job-seekers may be at risk of targeting by malicious actors looking for personal data. Brex recruiters will only reach out via LinkedIn or email with a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://brex.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://brex.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;brex.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;domain. Any outreach claiming to be from Brex via other sources should be ignored.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI &amp;amp; Analytics pillar powers how Klaviyo&#39;s customers understand their business, trust their data, and take action on insights. Our work spans the full analytics stack: from the foundational reporting infrastructure that every team at Klaviyo builds on top of, to AI-powered experiences that help marketers understand performance, explore their data, and take action — all from within the Klaviyo platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Klaviyo expands into Enterprise, Omnichannel, and AI-driven marketing, our analytics platform is evolving to match. That means modernizing the infrastructure underneath reporting, building AI experiences that are genuinely trustworthy and differentiated, and extending analytics to serve the needs of multi-brand Enterprise customers for the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Product Manager to own Klaviyo&#39;s Analytics AI product area — a cluster of tightly connected product challenges at the intersection of AI, data infrastructure, and analytics UX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary and largest ownership area is the &lt;strong&gt;Analytics Agent&lt;/strong&gt;: Klaviyo&#39;s in-product AI inside Composer that answers performance questions, surfaces insights, and serves as the shared intelligence foundation that every other Expert Agent in Klaviyo relies on for data grounding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How do you build an AI that gives answers a marketer can trust — ones that match the numbers already in the app? How do you go beyond returning metrics to delivering the &quot;why&quot; and the recommended next action? How do you reach data that generic LLMs over public APIs structurally cannot, and translate complex query infrastructure into simple, intuitive experiences that customers actually use? These are the questions this role is organized around.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond the Analytics Agent, this PM will own AI-native analytics UX (data visualization skills, AI-generated dashboards), the PM-side of Klaviyo&#39;s query infrastructure modernization, multi-brand organization analytics experiences, and ongoing platform health for core reporting surfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-visibility, high-leverage seat. The work you deliver will be felt across Klaviyo&#39;s entire agentic product suite, the Analytics SKU, and the Enterprise customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make a Difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own strategy and H2+ roadmap execution for the Analytics Agent across five pillars: Trust (quality, correctness, and reaching parity), Intelligence (metrics → insight → recommendation → action), Breadth (expanding to data that public APIs can&#39;t reach), Foundation (agent-as-a-tool architecture for Composer&#39;s multi-agent orchestration layer), and Experience (AI-generated charts, dashboards, and proactive in-context insights)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the quality measurement system for the Analytics Agent — design evals, LLM-as-judge scoring, and a golden set of production cases so the team can measure quality improvements reliably every week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own AI-generated analytics UX: define the right integration model between Composer&#39;s charting infrastructure, Core Reporting, and Analytics AI; ship a coherent NLI-driven visualization and dashboard creation experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the PM-side of Klaviyo&#39;s query infrastructure transition — as query execution engine migrates and new analytics capabilities become possible, define what that unlocks for customers, sequence migration priorities by customer value, and ensure the transition doesn&#39;t create gaps in existing surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the hiring manager on multi-account analytics &amp;amp; activation experiences for Enterprise Organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to drive multi-team alignment across a fast-moving, architecturally complex product area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear, rigorous product specs for AI behaviors, data-heavy features, and platform-level changes — artifacts that reflect deep understanding of edge cases, data semantics, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accountability for the health, quality, and steady-state reliability of core reporting surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3–5+ years of product management experience, with a strong track record of independently owning complex, multi-stakeholder product areas from strategy through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have direct, hands-on experience building AI or ML-powered products — not just products that use AI as a feature, but products where model quality, evaluation, and data grounding were core PM responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong data and analytics product background — you&#39;ve built or owned analytics, reporting, data visualization, or BI products and you care deeply about data accuracy, metric consistency, and customer trust in data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have demonstrated UX judgment for complex data experiences: you translate hard query infrastructure problems into simple, intuitive user-facing patterns, and you have a strong opinion on what makes a great data product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable working alongside major platform migrations or infrastructure transitions and can translate technical architecture shifts into product decisions and customer-value sequencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can influence multi-team roadmaps without direct authority — you&#39;ve navigated competing priorities across platform, feature, and infrastructure teams and made things move&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write clear, rigorous product specs for data-heavy and AI features — your artifacts reflect deep understanding of edge cases, failure modes, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re technically fluent enough to reason about LLM-based systems (evals, agent architecture, tool-use, retrieval), query infrastructure (semantic layers, schema design, query performance), and how they connect to customer-facing product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior ownership of an in-product AI assistant, chatbot, or analytics agent in a B2B SaaS context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing agent-to-agent interfaces or building products within a multi-agent orchestration system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with semantic data layers, query abstraction, or analytics infrastructure modernization projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in e-commerce, martech, or CDPs/CRMs, or marketing analytics — you understand how marketers think about campaign performance, attribution, and audience analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with data engineering or data platform teams as a PM partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Enterprise or upmarket customers with complex, multi-account or multi-brand data needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary range reflects the cost of labor across various U.S. geographic markets. The range displayed below reflects the minimum and maximum target salaries for the position across all our US locations. The base salary offered for this position is determined by several factors, including the applicant’s job-related skills, relevant experience, education or training, and work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, our total compensation package may include participation in the company’s annual cash bonus plan, variable compensation (OTE) for sales and customer success roles, equity, sign-on payments, and a comprehensive range of health, welfare, and wellbeing benefits based on eligibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruiter can provide more details about the specific salary/OTE range for your preferred location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range For US Locations:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$204,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may require up to 10% travel for purposes such as new hire onboarding, client or partner work if applicable, team meetings, and industry events. Travel is coordinated in advance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Klaviyo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Klaviyo (pronounced clay-vee-oh). We empower creators to own their destiny by making first-party data accessible and actionable like never before. We see limitless potential for the technology we’re developing to nurture personalized experiences in ecommerce and beyond. To reach our goals, we need our own crew of remarkable creators—ambitious and collaborative teammates who stay focused on our north star: delighting our customers. If you’re ready to do the best work of your career, where you’ll be welcomed as your whole self from day one and supported with generous benefits, we hope you’ll join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI fluency at Klaviyo includes responsible use of AI (including privacy, security, bias awareness, and human-in-the-loop). We provide accommodations as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By participating in Klaviyo’s interview process, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and will adhere to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/careers/ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.klaviyo.com/careers/ai-guidance&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1761072778777000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw0auUcRqeYRczM9UoXAKldj&quot;&gt;Guidelines for using AI in the Klaviyo interview Process&lt;/a&gt;. For more information about how we process your personal data, see our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.klaviyo.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1761072778777000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1axMoReIM1qwTbmaPcLI_b&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
